{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sally's Health and Wellness Column", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Believe It or Not", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe unusual events through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Past Continuous Tense and the Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"italic\">Past Continuous</span> tense to talk about an action that was happening at a time before now.  <br/>You use the <span class=\"italic\">Simple Past</span> to talk about a finished past action.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"italic\">Past Continuous</span> to:<ul><li>Describe the atmosphere at a particular time in the past.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">The children <span class=\"strong\">were laughing</span> and the birds <span class=\"strong\">were singing</span> in the park. A woman <span class=\"strong\">was looking</span> for her phone, which she dropped somewhere ...</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>Describe an action that was interrupted by another event or action.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">While they <span class=\"strong\">were playing</span> freely for an hour they were watched by an observer.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The form of the <span class=\"italic\">Past Continuous</span> is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">was</span>/<span class=\"italic\">were</span> + verb <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"italic\">Simple Past</span> to talk about a shorter action or event that happened in the middle of, or interrupted, the longer action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">They were taking turns, sharing toys, and helping each other when <span class=\"strong\">the researchers came into the room</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Researchers in a recent study were trying to find out if \"positive\" cartoons would have a good effect on children.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "While they were playing freely for an hour, they were watched by an observer who sat in the classroom and wrote down positive things they did. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They were taking turns, sharing toys, and helping each other. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Passive Voice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the active voice when you want the '<span class=\"italic\">doer</span>' of the action to be the subject. <br/>You use the passive voice when you want the '<span class=\"italic\">receiver</span>' of the action to be the subject.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Active sentence = <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"italic\">TV (subject) </span><span class=\"strong\">affects</span> kids' sleep, weight, grades, behavior and more (object). </span> </span><br/> Passive sentence = <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"italic\">Kids' sleep, weight, grades, behavior and more (subject) </span><span class=\"strong\">are affected</span> by TV (object) </span></span>. <br/><br/>  It is not always necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. <br/><br/>  You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the <span class=\"italic\">be</span> verb followed by the past participle. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Present passive form is:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">am</span>/<span class=\"italic\">are</span>/<span class=\"italic\">is</span> + past participle<br/><br/>  For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Children between the ages of three and five <span class=\"strong\">are shown</span> positive cartoons.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Past passive form is:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">was</span>/<span class=\"italic\">were </span>+ past participle<br/><br/>  For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Children between the ages of three and five <span class=\"strong\">were shown</span> positive cartoons.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">modal verbs</span> in the passive voice, too.<br/> You use modal verbs to add meaning to other verbs. <br/>They come before the dictionary form (Infinitive without '<span class=\"italic\">to</span>') of the main verb. <br/> Modal verbs can add meaning connected with possibility, certainty or obligation.<br/><br/>  For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Children between the ages of three and five <span class=\"strong\">should be shown</span> positive cartoons.</span><br/><br/>  Here the sentence now has an additional meaning of possibility, thanks to the modal verb <span class=\"italic\">should</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What can be done about the issue of violent cartoons for kids?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There aren't any limits on cartoons, which are usually shown in the afternoon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Forty children between the ages of three and five were shown positive cartoons. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They were watched by an observer who sat in the classroom and wrote down positive things they did. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to limit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to restrict; to create restrictions", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Some parents limit the amount of TV their children watch every day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about staying healthy.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "advisory ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an announcement that tells the public about the contents of a television program", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Television stations show an advisory.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to share", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to divide or distribute in equal parts", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Children were sharing toys.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to cooperate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to work together for a common benefit", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Cartoon characters cooperated in some way.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take turns", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do things in an organized way, with the participation of all members in a group", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Children were taking turns.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cooperative ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "showing mutual work, with benefits for everybody", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: TV can educate children to be either violent or cooperative. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online or visit a library. Try to find a popular English cartoon.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Watch an episode.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a short description of the episode, using the Past Continuous and Simple Past tenses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss the episode with a partner. Share your opinion of it.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I watch an English cartoon.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a short description of the episode.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss the episode with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my opinion about an English cartoon.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about staying healthy.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what was happening when something else happened. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can organize points in an argument.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you think that what children watch on TV or in movies influences how they behave in real life? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "  What is your opinion on video games? Do you think they are too violent? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "What can be done about TV violence?", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "STI", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"content